From: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: track the FPM generation on locally learned MACs

fpmsyncd replays every local MAC after an FPM connect, stamping each with a
generation carried in nlmsg_seq, then sends RTM_FPM_MAC_REPLAY_END. Without
per-MAC generation state zebra cannot tell which of its FPM-learned MACs
survived the reconnect, so entries that disappeared while the channel was
down keep being advertised.

Add a flag marking a MAC as FPM-learned and a field holding the generation it
was last refreshed in, so the end-of-replay handler can delete the entries
left behind by a previous session.

Signed-off-by: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
---
diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.h b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.h
index d854233810..ad2e8f590e 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.h
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mac.h
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ struct zebra_mac {
 #define ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE 0x800
 /* The MAC entry was created because of advertise_svi_mac */
 #define ZEBRA_MAC_SVI 0x1000
+/* The MAC was learned over the FPM channel rather than from the kernel. */
+#define ZEBRA_MAC_FPM_LEARNED 0x2000
 
 #define ZEBRA_MAC_ALL_LOCAL_FLAGS (ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL | ZEBRA_MAC_LOCAL_INACTIVE)
 #define ZEBRA_MAC_ALL_PEER_FLAGS                                               \
@@ -129,6 +131,11 @@ struct zebra_mac {
 	 */
 	uint32_t sync_neigh_cnt;
 
+	/* Generation this MAC was last refreshed in; only meaningful when
+	 * ZEBRA_MAC_FPM_LEARNED is set. Swept at end of replay.
+	 */
+	uint32_t fpm_generation;
+
 	time_t uptime;
 };
 
